<title>UK: ICCO lists buffer stock cocoa for sale in February.</title>
<headline>ICCO lists buffer stock cocoa for sale in February.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The buffer stock manager of the International Cocoa Organization (ICCO) announced on Wednesday the buffer stock sales planned for February would total a maximum 4,250 tonnes and would comprise the following cocoa, an ICCO press release said.</p>
<p>The date of the sale has yet to be announced.</p>
<p>Details of the cocoa offered for sale on description are as follows.</p>
<p> TONNES   ORIGIN	     PORT	 CROP    QUALITY</p>
<p>     6   Cote d'Ivoire   Amsterdam   1979/80   FF</p>
<p>   100   Cote d'Ivoire   Amsterdam   1981/82   GF</p>
<p>    76   Cote d'Ivoire   Amsterdam   1982/83   GF</p>
<p>   152   Cote d'Ivoire   Amsterdam   1982/83   FF</p>
<p>   101   Cote d'Ivoire   Amsterdam   1987/88   GF</p>
<p>    51   Cote d'Ivoire   Amsterdam   1987/88   FF</p>
<p>   582   Nigeria	   Amsterdam   1980/81   GF</p>
<p> 2,023   Nigeria	   Amsterdam   1980/81   FF</p>
<p>   131   Nigeria	   Amsterdam   1986/87   GF</p>
<p>The following parcels to be sold as per parcek drawn and approved by buyers.</p>
<p>	     WAREHOUSE					KEEPER</p>
<p>   501   Cote d'Ivoire Amsterdam  1981/82 FAQ Ocean Warehousing</p>
<p>							    (H.D. Cotterell)</p>
<p>    99   Cote d'Ivoire Amsterdam  1987/88 FAQ  Nedveem b.v.</p>
<p>   100   Cote d'Ivoire Amsterdam  1987/88 FAQ Handelsveem b.v.</p>
<p>   126   Cote d'Ivoire Rotterdam  1981/82 FAQ Ocean Warehousing</p>
<p>							    (H.D. Cotterell)</p>
<p>   203   Nigeria	 Amsterdam  1980/81 FAQ Ocean Warehousing</p>
<p>							    (H.D. Cotterell)</p>
<p>-- Clelia Oziel, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8072</p>
</text>
